wSource:'Show Markdown',openResult:'Open formatted result',chooseFile:'Choose a material',clearFocus:'Change focus',planDone:'All steps in this example are complete.',preparedReply:'## Prepared example reply\n\nThe task can become a verifiable plan:\n\n1. **Clarify the goal:** the result the human needs.\n2. **Gather materials:** decisions, source data and constraints.\n3. **Review the result:** compare the outcome with the acceptance criteria.\n\n> This is a prepared demonstration workflow. Your entered text is preserved in the message above.\n\n| Output | How to verify |\n|---|---|\n| Brief plan | A goal, a result and three steps are present |\n| Working document | It can be opened and edited |',prompt:'Create a project brief: the goal, stages and acceptance criteria. Save decisions in a document so the team can continue the work.',
    answer:'## From a discussion to a working plan\n\n**Goal:** prepare a clear project proposal and review it before implementation.\n\n### What is already agreed\n\n- One document keeps the goal and accepted decisions.\n- A plan shows the next action and its owner.\n- Review compares the result with the human’s expectations.\n\n| Stage | Output | Review |\n|---|---|---|\n| Definition | Project brief | The goal is clear without verbal explanation |\n| Execution | Working example | The main scenario can be explored |\n| Acceptance | Human decision | Each criterion is verified |\n\n> Agreement: when the goal changes, update the plan before continuing.\n\n### How the task progresses\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A["Human goal"] --> B["Plan and materials"]\n  B --> C["Working result"]\n  C --> D{"Criteria met?"}\n  D -->|Yes| E["Acceptance"]\n  D -->|Refine| B\n```\n\n### A verifiable task\n\n```yaml\ngoal: agree on the project plan\noutput: a short working document\nreview:\n  - goal is stated\n  - stages are defined\n  - criteria are agreed\n```\n\nThe document on the right already contains a detailed example. Open its editor or inspect the Markdown source.',
    brief:'# Project brief\n\n> **Expected result:** a person opens the workspace, understands the goal and finds the next step without retelling the whole story.\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nBring the discussion, materials and decisions together around one task. The conversation establishes agreement, the document records the result and the plan preserves the order of work.\n\n### Participants\n\n- **Task owner** defines the goal and accepts the result.\n- **Contributor** follows the plan and shares intermediate work.\n- **Reviewer** checks the result against agreed criteria.\n\n## 2. Deliverables\n\n| Material | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| Project brief | Agree on the goal and scope |\n| Working example | Review the primary scenario |\n| Acceptance checklist | Make completion verifiable |\n\n## 3. Sequence\n\n1. Clarify the task and initial constraints.\n2. Build the first complete example.\n3. Review it from the user’s perspective.\n4. Record the decision and next step.\n\n## 4. Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The goal and expected result are recorded.\n- [x] Materials are available from the workspace.\n- [ ] A human has explored the primary scenario.\n- [ ] Feedback is resolved and the decision is recorded.\n\n---\n\n**Working principle:** a new clarification updates the shared plan and related materials. The discussion history remains available.',
    research:'# Research findings\n\n## Observation\n\nParticipants can join a task more easily when its goal, materials and decisions are close together. This is an illustrative observation for demonstrating formatting.\n\n| Question | What to check |\n|---|---|\n| Is the goal clear? | A person can describe the expected result |\n| Are materials available? | The needed document opens from context |\n| Is the next step visible? | The plan names an immediate action |\n\n### Next experiment\n\n1. Give a person a short task.\n2. Ask them to open the plan and its related document.\n3. Record questions that arise.\n\n> An observation becomes a decision after review and discussion.',
    glossary:'# Project glossary\n\n| Term | Meaning in this work |\n|---|---|\n| Goal | A change a person needs |\n| Task | Specific work with a verifiable result |\n| Material | A document or data useful for a task |\n| Context | Agreements that influence decisions |\n| Acceptance | A human review of the result |\n\n## How to use it\n\nConsistent terms connect the conversation, plan and documents. Clarifying a definition prevents different interpretations of the same task.',
    transcript:'# Meeting transcript\n\n**Illustrative material · English translation**\n\n**Task owner:** Let’s first agree on what we want to achieve. I need a short document with the goal and steps.\n\n**Contributor:** We can record three stages: definition, a working example and review. Each gets an expected output.\n\n**Task owner:** Yes. The next person should also be able to continue without another explanation.\n\n## Meeting decisions\n\n- Prepare a project brief.\n- Connect the plan to working materials.\n- Accept the result after exploring the primary scenario.\n\n> Recording and speech processing belong to the separate BabelVoice tool. This demonstration uses a prepared transcript.',
    memoryText:'# Task memory\n\n## Accepted agreements\n\n- **Core:** a human sets the goal; the result is checked against agreed criteria.\n- **Format:** project brief + working example + checklist.\n- **Continuation:** a new participant starts from the current document.\n\n## Current considerations\n\n| Context | Effect on the work |\n|---|---|\n| Acceptance through the interface | Show the complete scenario |\n| Materials beside the discussion | Link the reply to a document |\n| A clear next step | Update the plan after a decision |',
    ontologyText:'# Relations in the working context\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  G["Goal"] -->|defines| T["Task"]\n  T -->|uses| M["Materials"]\n  T -->|creates| R["Result"]\n  C["Criteria"] -->|review| R\n  R -->|refines| M\n```\n\n| Relation | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| A task uses a material | A source document is needed for the work |\n| A task creates a result | The work produces a verifiable outcome |\n| Criteria review a result | Completion is checked against expectations |',
    plans:[['Clarify the goal','Record the result and constraints.'],['Build a working example','Connect the conversation, document and plan.'],['Review with a human','Explore the scenario and record the decision.']],agents:[['Coordinator','Breaks the goal into a sequence of tasks.','An agreed plan'],['Contributor','Creates a working result from the materials.','A document and an example'],['Reviewer','Checks the outcome independently of execution.','Observations and a decision']],boardColumns:['Next','In progress','Done'],boardCards:[['Review the scenario','Follow the task through to the document.'],['Prepare an example','Connect conclusions and materials.'],['Record the goal','The goal and criteria are recorded.']],bookmarks:[['Format agreement','Project brief + working example + checklist.'],['Acceptance criteria','Every stage has an expected output.']],
